{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Visual prompt + eval review surface (WS-VISUAL-EVAL)\n\n## Context\n\nSplit out of the workflow-engine remediation epic `soupy-spool-revel` (6f2d) as an\nexplicit, separately-scoped decision+build. Today Langfuse (optional, when keys set)\ngives a prompt-management + trace UI, and the `[eval]` extra wires Inspect/promptfoo\n(each with their own viewers), but there is no first-class, documented surface for a\nhuman to review prompts AND their eval STATUS together. The original epic framed this\nas a candidate/decision workstream; this epic owns deciding it and, if approved,\nbuilding it.\n\n## Why\n\nPrompt edits are gated by evals (see 6f2d WS-EVAL-EXISTING), but reviewers/maintainers\nhave no single place to see \"this prompt + its latest eval scores + kappa alignment +\nrecent traces\" together. The decision is whether to make this first-class (and on what\nsubstrate: Langfuse vs Inspect vs promptfoo vs a generated report) or to deliberately\nkeep the per-tool viewers and document that stance.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Decide: first-class surface vs keep-per-tool-viewers (ADR).\n- If first-class: choose substrate; decide whether `a88f`'s \"Langfuse = trace sink only\"\n  scoping should widen to prompt-management + eval status.\n- Preserve the engine invariants (git-native prompts, clean diffs, schema-validated text).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] ADR authored under `docs/adr/` recording the visual prompt+eval-review decision.\n- [ ] Decision references the eval seam delivered by 6f2d WS-EVAL-EXISTING.\n- [ ] If \"build\": the surface is implemented behind optional extras and documented in `docs/`.\n- [ ] If \"no build\": the rationale for keeping per-tool viewers is documented and the WS is closed.\n- [ ] A recorded decision (ADR) with rationale and rejected alternatives.\n- [ ] If build is chosen: a documented, reproducible surface a human can open to review"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785007152119073001,"uuid":"7c40cbfd-28de-4e99-a79f-11ae7bc41992"}